|errata_history=This is the original printed text (version 1 of 3). The image here is the Players Committee card image of the 2018 release ([[:File:V9-L-Odin_Nesloor_and_First_Aid-original-2018.gif]]). The current text is [[Odin Nesloor & •First Aid (Errata 2)]] (PC-E2). Each version below is quoted in full with its dated source; bracketed names such as [Immune to Alter.] stand for icons printed on the cards, and ▲ is the card's icon for “take into hand from Reserve Deck; reshuffle”.
* '''Original''' (this page): Virtual Set 9 release, 6 July 2018 ([[Virtual Set 9]]); Players Committee card image<ref name="ht-2018">[https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/022435b7929e4de26dafbcb1de2ec1d6d04d2153/Images-HT/starwars/Virtual9-Light/large/odinnesloorfirstaid.gif odinnesloorfirstaid.gif] in the PC's Holotable image repository (the images served at res.starwarsccg.org), commit 022435b "Set 9 load", 8 July 2018.</ref>: “If your character is about to be hit, use 1 Force (free if by a [Permanent Weapon] weapon) to prevent its forfeit from being reduced (and character is immune to Dr. Evazan) for remainder of turn. OR Cancel Disarmed. [Immune to Sense.] OR Cancel a ‘react.’ OR During your move phase, target any or all of your characters at one site to ‘transport’ (relocate) to an exterior or battleground site. Draw destiny. Use that much Force to ‘transport,’ or place Interrupt in Lost Pile.” No errata mark. A CardMaker recreation of this text ([[:File:V9-L-Odin_Nesloor_and_First_Aid-original-cardmaker.png]]) was made before this image was found and is no longer used.
* '''PC-E1''' ([[Odin Nesloor & •First Aid (Errata)]]): Errata Sheet 2021 Spring (official text as of 19 March 2021)<ref name="errata-2021-03">[https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/errata_032021.pdf#page=2 Errata Sheet 2021 Spring] (Players Committee, "Official text as of March 19, 2021"; PDF built 14 March 2021), page 2, Light Side. Preserved copy: [https://web.archive.org/web/20211005195534/https://res.starwarsccg.org/virtual/errata_032021.pdf Internet Archive]</ref> and the Players Committee card image<ref name="ht-2021">[https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/35aa2a66de8c2b5feeb1ad348a3a240cdc9ffbef/Images-HT/starwars/Virtual9-Light/large/odinnesloorfirstaid.gif odinnesloorfirstaid.gif] in the PC's Holotable image repository (the images served at res.starwarsccg.org), commit 35aa2a6 "updates from hires", 28 March 2021.</ref>, both marked “E”: “If your character is about to be hit, use 1 Force (free if by a [Permanent Weapon] weapon); for remainder of turn, its forfeit may not be reduced, it may not be used to satisfy attrition, and it is immune to Dr. Evazan. OR Cancel Disarmed. [Immune to Sense.] OR Cancel a 'react.' OR During your move phase, target any or all of your characters at one site to 'transport' (relocate) to an exterior or battleground site. Draw destiny. Use that much Force to 'transport,' or place Interrupt in Lost Pile.” '''What changed:''' “to prevent its forfeit from being reduced (and character is immune to Dr. Evazan) for remainder of turn” became “; for remainder of turn, its forfeit may not be reduced, it may not be used to satisfy attrition, and it is immune to Dr. Evazan” (the attrition clause is new); the curly quote marks of 2018 became straight ones ('react.', 'transport'). The sheet slip and the card image were published together for the same errata with the same words and mark, so they are recorded as one version.
* '''PC-E2''' ([[Odin Nesloor & •First Aid (Errata 2)]]): Players Committee card image, marked “E1”<ref name="ht-2022">[https://github.com/swccgpc/holotable/blob/6489b69/Images-HT/starwars/Virtual9-Light/large/odinnesloorfirstaid.gif odinnesloorfirstaid.gif] in the PC's Holotable image repository (the images served at res.starwarsccg.org), commit 6489b69 "Fixing case and making gifs", 10 July 2022.</ref>: “If your character is about to be hit, use 1 Force (free if by a [Permanent Weapon] weapon); for remainder of turn, its forfeit may not be reduced, it may not be used to satisfy attrition, and it is immune to Dr. Evazan. OR Cancel Disarmed. [Immune to Sense.] OR Cancel a ‘react.’ OR During your move phase, target any or all of your characters at one site to 'transport' (relocate) to an exterior or battleground site. Draw destiny. Use that much Force to 'transport,' or place Interrupt in Lost Pile.” '''What changed:''' the errata mark changed from “E” to “E1”; 'react.' is printed with curly quote marks again (‘react.’), while 'transport' keeps straight ones; line breaks moved. A version because the change is visible on the card (Bill, 12 November 2026). An image of 5 July 2022 (commit a41bae9 "fixing sizes") only changed the image size, with the same words and “E” mark, and is not counted. This is the current text.
|hatnote=For the current text, see [[Odin Nesloor & •First Aid (Errata 2)]].
}}